from pathlib import Path
import json
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
data={g:json.loads((P/f'{g}-manifest.json').read_text())['states'] for g in ('bare','helmet')}
page='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Veld west seated candidate</title><style>body{background:#202a30;color:#e1e7eb;font:16px system-ui;margin:24px}a{color:#8cc6e7}p{max-width:80ch;line-height:1.5}.row{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap}.card{background:#26353d;padding:12px}label,button,select{font:inherit}button,select{background:#344b57;color:white;padding:8px;border:1px solid #647f8e}canvas{display:block}.controls{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}</style>
<h1>Veld — west seated poses</h1><p>Independent left-facing source, one standing anatomy ruler and one pooled master material grade. The selected helmet is fitted at its original size and colour. Standing entry is the exact selected master; rising reverses the lowering poses. This is a staged candidate; chair contact and final motion acceptance remain pending.</p>
<div class="controls"><label>Equipment <select id="gear"><option value="bare">Bare</option><option value="helmet">Helmet</option></select></label><label>Action <select id="clip"><option value="0">Sit down</option><option value="1">Rise</option><option value="2">Seated</option></select></label><button id="play">Pause</button><label>Frame <input id="slot" type="range" min="0" max="5" value="0"></label><span id="status">Loading</span></div>
<div class="row"><div class="card"><strong>Selected standing master</strong><canvas id="master" width="256" height="256"></canvas></div><div class="card"><strong>Current pose</strong><canvas id="pose" width="256" height="256"></canvas></div><div class="card"><strong>Gameplay scale</strong><canvas id="small" width="200" height="256"></canvas></div></div>
<p>Playback is slowed to one-third speed. Finite actions stop at their terminal pose; press Replay to restart.</p><p><a href="paired-contact.png">Both equipment variants and close-ups</a> · <a href="source-review.png">Ungraded source against master</a> · <a href="sources/seated-v1.png">Original source atlas</a> · <a href="native-review.png">Actual sprite player capture</a> · <a href="HANDOFF.md">Review scope and remaining work</a></p>
<h2>All four directions</h2><p>Source-only comparison at one shared scale and clock. East and west seated heights are close; the taller south pose and shorter north pose need further anatomy and chair-contact review. Different views need not have identical bounding boxes.</p><img src="family-motion.gif" width="1024" style="max-width:100%;height:auto" alt="Four directions replaying lowering, seated hold and rising in bare and helmet variants"><p><a href="family-review.png">Standing, lowering and seated comparison</a> · <a href="family-review.json">Measurements and source bindings</a></p>
<script>const data=DATA;let images={},playing=true,elapsed=0,last=performance.now(),slot=0;const gear=document.querySelector('#gear'),clip=document.querySelector('#clip'),range=document.querySelector('#slot'),play=document.querySelector('#play'),status=document.querySelector('#status');
function reset(){elapsed=0;slot=0;range.value=0;range.max=data[gear.value][Number(clip.value)].frameFiles.length-1;playing=true;play.textContent='Pause'}gear.onchange=reset;clip.onchange=reset;
range.oninput=()=>{slot=Number(range.value);playing=false;play.textContent='Replay'};play.onclick=()=>{if(playing){playing=false;play.textContent='Replay'}else reset()};
function load(path){return new Promise((yes,no)=>{const im=new Image();im.onload=()=>yes(im);im.onerror=()=>no(Error(path));im.src=path+'?v=west-fit-v1'})}
Promise.all(Object.values(data).flat().flatMap(s=>s.frameFiles).filter((v,i,a)=>a.indexOf(v)===i).map(async p=>images[p]=await load(p))).then(()=>{
function draw(now){if(playing)elapsed+=(now-last)/3;last=now;const state=data[gear.value][Number(clip.value)];if(playing){slot=0;let t=elapsed;while(slot<state.frameFiles.length-1&&t>=state.frameDurationsMs[slot])t-=state.frameDurationsMs[slot++];if(elapsed>=state.frameDurationsMs.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)){playing=false;play.textContent='Replay'}range.value=slot}
const im=images[state.frameFiles[slot]],master=images[data[gear.value][0].frameFiles[0]];for(const [id,source] of [['master',master],['pose',im]]){const c=document.querySelector('#'+id).getContext('2d');c.clearRect(0,0,256,256);c.drawImage(source,0,0)}const c=document.querySelector('#small').getContext('2d');c.clearRect(0,0,200,256);c.drawImage(im,0,90,142,142);c.drawImage(im,142,185,47,47);status.textContent=`Frame ${slot} · ${state.id}`;requestAnimationFrame(draw)}requestAnimationFrame(draw)}).catch(e=>status.textContent='Missing image: '+e.message);</script>'''
(P/'index.html').write_text(page.replace('DATA',json.dumps(data)),encoding='utf-8')
print('Master/pose/small-scale candidate review page saved.')
